{:db/id 17592186092264 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186092120 :question/id #uuid "5d2c0fff-c9af-5e8a-846a-640878f08283" :question/math-academy-id "e-730" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $f(x) = \\ln(x^2-4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf = \\ln u, \\qquad u = x^2-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = \\dfrac{1}{u},\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm d x} = 2x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac7f7e-1e07-57d7-a82a-d6545588c2de" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186050690} {:db/id 17592186051084}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186092514 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d52c6551-fc4a-5676-a7d0-b9c0cc8678e3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x^{2}}{x^{3} - 4}" :db/id 17592186089256} {:answer/id #uuid "061c6223-674b-5aec-92fb-4a26c9907ef4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{x^{3} - 4}" :db/id 17592186089257} {:answer/id #uuid "1783ab77-0c34-5273-8e3b-4e40ed8e7e68" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\ln (x^{3} - 4)" :db/id 17592186089258} {:answer/id #uuid "5db05ff3-38fb-58d4-88fc-c482329f0811" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{x^{3} - 4}" :db/id 17592186089259} {:answer/id #uuid "70794b27-6bac-5e9a-9c47-8ed2c45960cd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{x^{3} - 4}" :db/id 17592186089260}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3b5a8912-02dc-578f-9bd6-8084a007e4a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186089255}] :question/id #uuid "5e2b43c8-15e7-5f90-9659-500eb6eb563c" :question/math-academy-id "q-11934" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = \\ln (x^{3} - 4)$, find $\\frac{df}{dx}$."} {:db/id 17592186092677 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a7b4309-5fd2-5174-94f7-5dfc02eb55bc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2x}" :db/id 17592186090279} {:answer/id #uuid "910dd200-ce6f-5abd-8148-fc49d5edf00b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x} + 1" :db/id 17592186090280} {:answer/id #uuid "93466ea8-4667-5103-99d9-daf38e58b163" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id 17592186090281} {:answer/id #uuid "14ee5a98-750c-5372-8840-e0127f0dc6cd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x} + 2" :db/id 17592186090282} {:answer/id #uuid "498ded3b-7d79-53b4-b85c-f13be90e5ef1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id 17592186090283}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b9690acc-cfe2-5e00-9615-bc8aa9eb8f79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186090278}] :question/id #uuid "4bf4a8f5-b101-5407-90c0-19deea0e2b6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-28632" :question/problem "For $g(x) = \\ln (2x)$, find $g^{′}(x)$."} {:db/id 17592186233100 :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e624a42e-febd-5a83-813e-03b578dd4b5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107469" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}(4-2x)$ at the point $(1,\\operatorname{ln}2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{ln}u,\\,u=4-2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-2x}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{4-2x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\cancel{2}}{\\cancel{2}\\cdot (2-x)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={-\\frac{1}{2-x}|}_{x=1}=-\\frac{1}{2-1}=-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(1,\\operatorname{ln}2)$ is $m=-1.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-\\operatorname{ln}2 & =-1(x-1) \\\\ y & =-x+1+\\operatorname{ln}2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186233916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4001bcd4-bb92-5556-b468-857dd559531f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{30{x}^{5}}{3-5{x}^{6}}" :db/id 17592186232846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4001bcd4-bb92-5556-b468-857dd559531f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{30{x}^{5}}{3-5{x}^{6}}" :db/id 17592186232846} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfd8924e-61f1-5f4c-a0c0-4e1e11def7af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186232845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b0416da-07ab-52a1-b4f0-696bed0ae814" :question/math-academy-id "q-341676" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}(3-5{x}^{6})$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{ln}u,\\,u=3-5{x}^{6}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-30{x}^{5}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-30{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-5{x}^{6}}\\cdot (-30{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{30{x}^{5}}{3-5{x}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186253563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cb5d83c-b113-5e49-8ad1-b7af79795399" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{x}" :db/id 17592186250661} {:answer/id #uuid "134a924c-2d79-5a81-a5e4-b32b5f6f1568" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8ln⁡8x" :db/id 17592186250720} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6aaf6a-f7c4-5c7f-bd3f-349e7ca5691e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{ln⁡8x}" :db/id 17592186251444} {:answer/id #uuid "de9d5bb2-c832-5736-b2a1-be6b5d245d22" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id 17592186252513} {:answer/id #uuid "e065e44d-7317-5a6d-9dae-1e8e400b8d8d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8x}" :db/id 17592186252529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de9d5bb2-c832-5736-b2a1-be6b5d245d22" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id 17592186252513} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a2d08ee-6e6a-5895-bb57-f6640a579319" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186253043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9e0ca00-8b2a-5d3e-84fd-62f2c13cf2f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11930" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=ln⁡(8x)$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here $f(x)=ln⁡(8x)$ is a function of a function. We use the chain rule.First, we express $g(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=8x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8x}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{8x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{8}}{\\cancel{8}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186253567 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d7b3388-0623-533e-bfdf-9f2c6f502040" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xln⁡{x}^{2}" :db/id 17592186250941} {:answer/id #uuid "416392e1-706e-5bf2-9d81-60e36e16385e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id 17592186251095} {:answer/id #uuid "997542b7-5b4e-5730-bcd9-42ca51f3257b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id 17592186251871} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ebb09a-1202-54dc-96e3-4ba8aa79086d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id 17592186252309} {:answer/id #uuid "d325e97e-1656-5db8-b154-544f8ba85d31" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id 17592186252423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6ebb09a-1202-54dc-96e3-4ba8aa79086d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id 17592186252309} :answer-field/id #uuid "49b60ab6-927a-5636-b89c-9078309c85cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186252934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ad2837f1-ee8d-5b88-b0b4-540909ba188a" :question/math-academy-id "q-11932" :question/problem "Given that $g(x)=ln⁡{x}^{2}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $g(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ng=ln⁡u,\\,u={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cancel{x}}{x\\cdot \\cancel{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186275257 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33827fd0-4534-55f0-97b2-d161bddcb638" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x+1" :db/id 17592186272845} {:answer/id #uuid "70fa2499-450b-5a01-ac51-9c973bf1c984" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x" :db/id 17592186273356} {:answer/id #uuid "9b9aa4f0-b3de-5ebd-a3bf-880c8f6adde9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x" :db/id 17592186273734} {:answer/id #uuid "b22cb302-cb5a-57cd-8771-68674690aed4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x+3" :db/id 17592186273925} {:answer/id #uuid "b77cc92e-a825-533b-b1a3-c4323ff6da05" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id 17592186273979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70fa2499-450b-5a01-ac51-9c973bf1c984" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x" :db/id 17592186273356} :answer-field/id #uuid "95e2d1b8-e241-5d42-adc2-c7b1c34e1e9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186274893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2b8ebe67-7d90-5f2a-b18d-1cdea332312f" :question/math-academy-id "q-150014" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x+1)$ at the point $(0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,u=3x+1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3x+1}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={\\frac{3}{3x+1}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3(0)+1} \\\\  & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(0,0)$ is $m=3.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =3\\cdot (x-0) \\\\ y & =3x\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186275258 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "197f7f3c-1814-5539-88cc-8d324898ee5c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x+1" :db/id 17592186272609} {:answer/id #uuid "2fea7db3-4e7c-5614-ae83-fa65014e2989" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x-1" :db/id 17592186272814} {:answer/id #uuid "6bfeaa14-af54-5709-b268-7fb92c5fb931" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+1" :db/id 17592186273318} {:answer/id #uuid "a60c1e22-63e1-5366-8ce8-00afd5a3b3bf" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x" :db/id 17592186273824} {:answer/id #uuid "db9385c8-9e1d-581c-b45b-9f71e6e47ebb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x" :db/id 17592186274313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bfeaa14-af54-5709-b268-7fb92c5fb931" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+1" :db/id 17592186273318} :answer-field/id #uuid "a555f44f-209a-564b-9155-a69db2cccbc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186274923}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "329ee6a2-6455-51c9-9cfd-81f75012b6f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-150015" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=ln⁡(2-x)$ at the point $(1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=2-x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-x}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={\\frac{1}{x-2}|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1)-2} \\\\  & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(1,0)$ is $m=-1.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =(-1)\\cdot (x-1) \\\\ y & =-x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186297318 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd3f823c-979f-5d9f-9a75-a1d72b9ea787" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{9}" :db/id 17592186296615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd3f823c-979f-5d9f-9a75-a1d72b9ea787" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{9}" :db/id 17592186296615} :answer-field/id #uuid "2796bd13-a599-55af-9fb2-de539c4e21ac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186296708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f22eb9bd-4b64-597a-920f-3c1311c73e8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-310144" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=ln⁡(5{x}^{2}+4)$ at the point where $x=1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=5{x}^{2}+4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=10x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 10x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5{x}^{2}+4}\\cdot 10x \\\\  & =\\frac{10x}{5{x}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=1} & ={\\frac{10x}{5{x}^{2}+4}|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10(1)}{5({1}^{2})+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186317167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "494a94d3-24b4-54af-9812-b43bf65d1ed8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id 17592186315539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "494a94d3-24b4-54af-9812-b43bf65d1ed8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id 17592186315539} :answer-field/id #uuid "08fcd987-267b-5991-8d3b-e7ba670ba940" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186316572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8869b9ad-0609-5467-9c5a-358cef5acc13" :question/math-academy-id "q-341671" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=ln⁡(9x)$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=9x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=9.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9x}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{9}}{\\cancel{9}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186317168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41009420-72ae-56fd-aa83-eccb8bd06467" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{11}" :db/id 17592186315494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41009420-72ae-56fd-aa83-eccb8bd06467" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{11}" :db/id 17592186315494} :answer-field/id #uuid "72e4d41f-0ef4-5057-b7b2-fa06aa4b75c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186316822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e7be6bd-4db9-564a-80e4-a31c43152284" :question/math-academy-id "q-341679" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=ln⁡(7-4x)$ at the point where $x=-1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=7-4x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7-4x}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7-4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=-1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=-1} & ={-\\frac{4}{7-4x}|}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7-4(-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{11}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186329899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c9f795a-fdf7-5960-9416-86b82de61eeb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-2-ln⁡8" :db/id 17592186327599} {:answer/id #uuid "a92a0dde-6864-5de5-a1e0-0756332b235c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-8+4ln⁡8" :db/id 17592186328401} {:answer/id #uuid "baa4f79f-eef4-5e8e-aac2-b20cd55f0ab6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x-4" :db/id 17592186328562} {:answer/id #uuid "cb545cef-1504-5ba6-adfa-85adecaf6377" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x-4+4ln⁡8" :db/id 17592186328716} {:answer/id #uuid "dadc186a-82fe-5292-9424-ff20b848c7a0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x+4" :db/id 17592186328848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb545cef-1504-5ba6-adfa-85adecaf6377" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x-4+4ln⁡8" :db/id 17592186328716} :answer-field/id #uuid "61aeee27-1516-5091-a830-2d16db15c76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186329356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "35dfe1cb-907d-5d3e-a83a-3ec0018cc2f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-48654" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=4ln⁡(2x)$ at the point $(4,4ln⁡8).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=4ln⁡u,\\,u=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{4}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{u}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2x}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 4}{\\cancel{2}\\cdot x} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=4$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4} & ={\\frac{4}{x}|}_{x=4}=\\frac{4}{4}=1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(4,4ln⁡8)$ is $m=1.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-4ln⁡(8) & =1(x-4) \\\\ y & =x-4+4ln⁡(8)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Natural Logarithm Function Using the Chain Rule"}